function.arguments:
{
  "note": "Conditional fit prototype, not a certified door repair. Flat-tread 50 × 16 mm split wheel for two nominal 608 bearings. Track profile, door support arrangement, load, bracket clearance and existing bolt length remain unknown. Do not install on a top-hung door or rely on it to retain a door. Do not put the door's weight on this prototype until compatibility and safe support have been established. PLA creep and wear make this unsuitable as an unqualified permanent replacement. A matching manufacturer-rated roller is preferred.",
  "questions": [
    {"text":"Track profile, mounting arrangement and whether the door is top-hung?","answer":"User could not measure; unknown."},
    {"text":"Existing bolt length, bracket thickness and door weight?","answer":"Not supplied. Existing shank is about 8 mm; this does not establish usable bolt length."}
  ],
  "params": {
    "wheel_d":{"value":50,"kind":"world","source":"asked","note":"Approximate original diameter, not verified."},
    "wheel_w":{"value":16,"kind":"world","source":"asked","note":"Approximate original width; excludes axle hardware."},
    "bearing_od":{"value":22,"kind":"hardware","source":"measured","note":"User reports about 22 mm; fit must be tested."},
    "bearing_w":{"value":7,"kind":"hardware","source":"measured","note":"User reports about 7 mm."},
    "bearing_bore":{"value":8,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog","note":"Nominal 608 bore."},
    "existing_shank_d":{"value":8,"kind":"hardware","source":"measured","note":"Approximate; existing bolt length and thread unknown."},
    "existing_bolt_length":{"value":null,"kind":"hardware","source":"unknown"},
    "bracket_stack":{"value":null,"kind":"world","source":"unknown"},
    "door_mass":{"value":null,"kind":"world","source":"unknown","note":"Not used to claim a load rating."},
    "bearing_fit_allowance":{"value":0.2,"kind":"design","source":"design","note":"Diametral clearance; slip fit, not press fit."},
    "centre_gap":{"value":0.8,"kind":"design","source":"design","note":"Inner-race spacer length; leaves 0.6 mm exterior retaining lips at nominal bearing widths."},
    "face_opening_d":{"value":16,"kind":"design","source":"design"},
    "spacer_od":{"value":11.5,"kind":"design","source":"design","note":"Must contact inner race only; verify against actual bearing, not seals."},
    "axle_clearance_d":{"value":8.5,"kind":"design","source":"design"},
    "outer_spacer_w":{"value":2,"kind":"design","source":"design"},
    "fastener_radius":{"value":17.5,"kind":"design","source":"design"},
    "fastener_count":{"value":3,"unit":"count","kind":"design","source":"design"},
    "m3_d":{"value":3,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog"},
    "m3_clearance":{"value":0.4,"kind":"design","source":"design"},
    "m3_head_d":{"value":5.5,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog"},
    "m3_head_h":{"value":3,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog"},
    "m3_head_clearance":{"value":0.5,"kind":"design","source":"design"},
    "m3_nut_af":{"value":5.5,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog"},
    "m3_nut_h":{"value":2.4,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog"},
    "nut_clearance":{"value":0.4,"kind":"design","source":"design"},
    "recess_depth":{"value":3.2,"kind":"design","source":"design"},
    "m3_length":{"value":12,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog"},
    "m8_length":{"value":30,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog","note":"Specified alternative axle, not identification of the user's bolt."},
    "m8_nut_h":{"value":8,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog","note":"ISO 10511 M8."},
    "m8_pitch":{"value":1.25,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog"},
    "m8_washer_t":{"value":1.6,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog"},
    "m8_washer_od":{"value":16,"kind":"hardware","source":"catalog"},
    "coupon_wall":{"value":3,"kind":"design","source":"design"},
    "coupon_h":{"value":3,"kind":"design","source":"design"}
  },
  "parts": [
    {
      "id":"bearing_fit_coupon","role":"coupon","material":"PLA",
      "code":"def build(p):\n    d=p.bearing_od+p.bearing_fit_allowance\n    return cq.Workplane('XY').circle(d/2+p.coupon_wall).circle(d/2).extrude(p.coupon_h)\n",
      "print_orientation":"Flat annular face on bed, z=0.",
      "use_orientation":"Test bearing outside diameter only; not part of assembly."
    },
    {
      "id":"wheel_head_half","role":"final","material":"PLA",
      "code":"import math\n\ndef build(p):\n    h=p.wheel_w/2\n    lip=(p.wheel_w-2*p.bearing_w-p.centre_gap)/2\n    if lip <= 0: raise ValueError('Insufficient wheel width for bearings and spacer')\n    s=cq.Workplane('XY').circle(p.wheel_d/2).extrude(h)\n    s=s.cut(cq.Workplane('XY').circle(p.face_opening_d/2).extrude(h))\n    s=s.cut(cq.Workplane('XY').workplane(offset=lip).circle((p.bearing_od+p.bearing_fit_allowance)/2).extrude(h-lip))\n    for i in range(int(p.fastener_count)):\n        a=2*math.pi*i/p.fastener_count\n        x,y=p.fastener_radius*math.cos(a),p.fastener_radius*math.sin(a)\n        s=s.cut(cq.Workplane('XY').center(x,y).circle((p.m3_d+p.m3_clearance)/2).extrude(h))\n        s=s.cut(cq.Workplane('XY').center(x,y).circle((p.m3_head_d+p.m3_head_clearance)/2).extrude(p.recess_depth))\n    return s\n",
      "print_orientation":"Exterior face z=0 on bed; large bearing pocket opens upward. Small underside head recess roofs bridge approximately 6 mm.",
      "use_orientation":"Assembly coordinates unchanged: exterior z=0; split face z=8."
    },
    {
      "id":"wheel_nut_half","role":"final","material":"PLA",
      "code":"import math\n\ndef build(p):\n    h=p.wheel_w/2\n    lip=(p.wheel_w-2*p.bearing_w-p.centre_gap)/2\n    if lip <= 0: raise ValueError('Insufficient wheel width for bearings and spacer')\n    s=cq.Workplane('XY').circle(p.wheel_d/2).extrude(h)\n    s=s.cut(cq.Workplane('XY').circle(p.face_opening_d/2).extrude(h))\n    s=s.cut(cq.Workplane('XY').workplane(offset=lip).circle((p.bearing_od+p.bearing_fit_allowance)/2).extrude(h-lip))\n    for i in range(int(p.fastener_count)):\n        a=2*math.pi*i/p.fastener_count\n        x,y=p.fastener_radius*math.cos(a),p.fastener_radius*math.sin(a)\n        s=s.cut(cq.Workplane('XY').center(x,y).circle((p.m3_d+p.m3_clearance)/2).extrude(h))\n        s=s.cut(cq.Workplane('XY').center(x,y).polygon(6,2*(p.m3_nut_af+p.nut_clearance)/math.sqrt(3)).extrude(p.recess_depth))\n    return s\n",
      "print_orientation":"Exterior face z=0 on bed; bearing pocket upward. Nut recess roofs bridge less than 7 mm.",
      "use_orientation":"Flip 180 degrees about X, then translate +16 mm in Z: split faces meet at assembly z=8. Align three screw holes."
    },
    {
      "id":"inner_spacer","role":"final","material":"PLA",
      "code":"def build(p):\n    return cq.Workplane('XY').circle(p.spacer_od/2).circle(p.axle_clearance_d/2).extrude(p.centre_gap)\n",
      "print_orientation":"Flat ring on bed, z=0; four layers at 0.2 mm.",
      "use_orientation":"Between the two bearing inner races, assembly z=7.6 to 8.4 at nominal dimensions."
    },
    {
      "id":"head_side_spacer","role":"final","material":"PLA",
      "code":"def build(p):\n    return cq.Workplane('XY').circle(p.spacer_od/2).circle(p.axle_clearance_d/2).extrude(p.outer_spacer_w)\n",
      "print_orientation":"Flat ring on bed.",
      "use_orientation":"On axle against first bearing inner race; projects beyond wheel face."
    },
    {
      "id":"nut_side_spacer","role":"final","material":"PLA",
      "code":"def build(p):\n    return cq.Workplane('XY').circle(p.spacer_od/2).circle(p.axle_clearance_d/2).extrude(p.outer_spacer_w)\n",
      "print_orientation":"Flat ring on bed.",
      "use_orientation":"On axle against second bearing inner race; projects beyond wheel face."
    }
  ],
  "hardware": [
    {"id":"bearings","ref":"608ZZ","qty":2},
    {"id":"wheel_screws","ref":"ISO 4762 M3x12","qty":3},
    {"id":"wheel_nuts","ref":"ISO 4032 M3","qty":3},
    {"id":"axle","ref":"ISO 4762 M8x30","qty":1},
    {"id":"axle_nut","ref":"ISO 10511 M8","qty":1},
    {"id":"axle_washers","ref":"ISO 7089 M8","qty":2}
  ],
  "joints": [
    {
      "id":"wheel_closure","fastener":"wheel_screws",
      "axis_origin":[17.5,0,3.2],"axis_dir":[0,0,1],
      "seats":[
        {"part":"wheel_head_half","feature":"Three cylindrical recess floors, repeated at 120 degrees; screw underside seats at assembly z=3.2.","role":"head_seat"},
        {"part":"wheel_head_half","feature":"Three 3.4 mm through holes.","role":"clearance"},
        {"part":"wheel_nut_half","feature":"Aligned through holes.","role":"clearance"},
        {"part":"wheel_nut_half","feature":"Three outward-opening hex pockets; assembly floors at z=12.8.","role":"nut_pocket"}
      ],
      "nut":"wheel_nuts"
    },
    {
      "id":"conditional_axle","fastener":"axle",
      "axis_origin":[0,0,-3],"axis_dir":[0,0,1],
      "seats":[
        {"part":"head_side_spacer","feature":"8.5 mm axial bore.","role":"clearance"},
        {"part":"inner_spacer","feature":"8.5 mm axial bore.","role":"clearance"},
        {"part":"nut_side_spacer","feature":"8.5 mm axial bore.","role":"clearance"}
      ],
      "nut":"axle_nut",
      "external":"Actual bracket is unmeasured. Axis origin assumes a bench stack with no bracket; installation requires a verified stack and accessibility."
    }
  ],
  "criteria": [
    {
      "id":"bearing_slip_fit","part":"wheel_head_half","feature":"22.2 mm bearing pocket","relation":"contains","hardware":"bearings","clearance_mm":0.2,
      "params":["bearing_od","bearing_fit_allowance"],
      "check":{"method":"coupon","ref":"bearing_fit_coupon","description":"Both bearings must enter by hand without forcing and without appreciable rocking. Adjust diametral allowance and reprint coupon if needed."}
    },
    {
      "id":"inner_race_contact","part":"inner_spacer","feature":"Spacer end faces","relation":"seats","hardware":"bearings",
      "params":["spacer_od","axle_clearance_d","centre_gap"],
      "check":{"method":"measure","description":"Confirm ring faces contact metal inner races only, not bearing shields or outer races. Reject if not verifiable. Spacer must sit flat and remain intact."}
    },
    {
      "id":"rotating_clearance","part":"head_side_spacer","feature":"Projection beyond wheel face","relation":"clears","hardware":"axle_washers",
      "params":["wheel_w","bearing_w","centre_gap","outer_spacer_w","face_opening_d"],
      "check":{"method":"measure","description":"Nominal spacer projection is 1.4 mm. Washers and bracket must not contact the wheel or bearing shields throughout rotation. Verify both sides."}
    },
    {
      "id":"track_fit","part":"wheel_head_half","feature":"Flat cylindrical tread and wheel envelope","relation":"supports",
      "params":["wheel_d","wheel_w"],
      "check":{"method":"template","description":"With door independently supported, compare assembled wheel to original and track without loading it. Flat tread is an unverified assumption. Reject for a groove, crown, flange requirement, interference or loss of retention."}
    },
    {
      "id":"axle_length_check","part":"nut_side_spacer","feature":"Complete stationary axle stack","relation":"engages","hardware":"axle",
      "params":["m8_length","bearing_w","centre_gap","outer_spacer_w","m8_washer_t","m8_nut_h","m8_pitch","bracket_stack"],
      "check":{"method":"measure","description":"Bench grip is 22 mm before nut: 14 mm bearings + 0.8 mm centre spacer + 4 mm outer spacers + 3.2 mm washers. M8x30 only reaches nominal end of an 8 mm nut with NO bracket, so is NOT approved for bracket installation. Installed bolt must exceed full grip plus bracket thickness plus 8 mm nut plus at least one 1.25 mm thread. Use only a verified suitable listed length; otherwise stop."}
    }
  ],
  "manual": [
    {"n":"1","text":"Secure the door independently so it cannot fall, tip or leave its track. Do not remove a supporting roller without appropriate support. If this is top-hung, or you cannot establish how the door is supported and retained, stop at bench testing and obtain the correct rated replacement."},
    {"n":"2","text":"Print bearing_fit_coupon at 0.2 mm layers and check both bearings. Use a hand slip fit, not a forced interference fit. Do not hammer bearings into PLA.","parts":["bearing_fit_coupon"],"hardware":["bearings"]},
    {"n":"3","text":"Print the six final parts in their specified orientations, 0.2 mm layers, at least six walls and 100% infill. No supports are needed; the small screw/nut recess roofs bridge under 7 mm. Remove burrs and inspect the thin exterior bearing-retention lips for missing layers or cracks.","parts":["wheel_head_half","wheel_nut_half","inner_spacer","head_side_spacer","nut_side_spacer"]},
    {"n":"4","text":"Lay wheel_head_half exterior face down. Seat one bearing in its upward pocket. Place inner_spacer on the inner race. Verify it touches only that race. Place the second bearing on the spacer, then lower the flipped wheel_nut_half over it. Align the screw holes. Bearings seat against the outside lips; their outer races are separated by 0.8 mm at nominal dimensions.","parts":["wheel_head_half","wheel_nut_half","inner_spacer"],"hardware":["bearings"]},
    {"n":"5","text":"Insert three M3 nuts into the exterior hex pockets and the three M3x12 screws from the opposite exterior face. Tighten evenly only until split faces meet and screws are snug. Nominal nut engagement is full 2.4 mm, with screw tips recessed. Stop if the split will not close, bearings bind, or PLA distorts. Recheck screw security frequently; no threadlocker is specified.","parts":["wheel_head_half","wheel_nut_half"],"hardware":["wheel_screws","wheel_nuts"],"tool":"2.5 mm hex key"},
    {"n":"6","text":"Bench axle order: M8 bolt head, washer, head_side_spacer, first bearing inner race, inner_spacer, second bearing inner race, nut_side_spacer, washer, locknut. Ensure the bearing bores slide onto the axle without force. The M8x30 is only a nominal bench-stack bolt: it has no length allowance for a bracket or a protruding thread. Do not interpret this as approval to install it on the door.","parts":["head_side_spacer","inner_spacer","nut_side_spacer"],"hardware":["axle","axle_washers","axle_nut","bearings"]},
    {"n":"7","text":"For any later mounting trial, first measure the bracket and axle stack. Require a verified M8 length giving full locknut engagement and at least one thread beyond the nut; use an appropriate listed ISO 4762 length only if it fits the actual mounting arrangement. The user's existing bolt is unidentified beyond approximate shank diameter. If a suitable axle cannot be verified, stop. Never tighten directly against the rotating wheel or outer bearing races.","hardware":["axle","axle_nut","axle_washers"]},
    {"n":"8","text":"Tighten the bench axle gently while turning the wheel. Only the inner races and spacers should be clamped. Stop if rotation becomes rough, the wheel rubs the washers, or spacers crush. Do not solve binding by leaving the axle loose. Printed spacers can creep and do not establish a permanent structural joint.","parts":["inner_spacer","head_side_spacer","nut_side_spacer"],"hardware":["axle","axle_nut"]},
    {"n":"9","text":"With the door still independently supported, compare the wheel's flat tread, diameter, width, side clearance and retention with the track and original roller. Any mismatch means reject this design. Do not put the door's weight on the prototype based on this fit check. Unknown load and track geometry prevent a safe service rating; obtain a matching rated roller for normal use.","parts":["wheel_head_half","wheel_nut_half"]}
  ]
}
